ernally from the beginning. \r\n\r\nSo if you can provide a smaller libcurl example that can make this happen without setting POSTFIELDS then I'm very curious!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/comments/462265732/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"bagder","id":177011,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzAxMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder","html_url":"https://github.com/bagder","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/comments/462297784","html_url":"https://github.com/curl/curl/issues/3548#issuecomment-462297784","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/3548","id":462297784,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2MjI5Nzc4NA==","user":{"login":"VMbonn","id":47519627,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NTE5NjI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47519627?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/VMbonn","html_url":"https://github.com/VMbonn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VMbonn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VMbonn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VMbonn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VMbonn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VMbonn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VMbonn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VMbonn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VMbonn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VMbonn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-02-11T11:36:48Z","updated_at":"2019-02-11T11:36:48Z","body":"Maybe the reason for the segmentation fault is, that a _previous_ call to the function 'httpRequest' uses the requerstType = POST. The pointer set by this _previous_ call using CURLOPT_POSTFIELDS is only valid during is call and was been freed by the caller. But from my point of view an invalid pointer to CURLOPT_POSTFIELDS must not have any impact to calls using GET.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/comments/462297784/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"VMbonn","id":47519627,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NTE5NjI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47519627?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/VMbonn","html_url":"https://github.com/VMbonn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VMbonn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VMbonn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VMbonn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VMbonn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VMbonn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VMbonn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VMbonn/repos","events_url":"htt